## Route 3: derivation from the jet basis {#sec:route3}

The third derivation (Section~\ref{sec:B}) constructs the Gaudin K tensor of $\Phi_c^\infty$ in the jet basis that replaces the SoV basis when $h\to0$, and finds exactly 25 non-zero entries on $N_5\times N_5$, equal to $G/(4\omega_1^3\omega_1'^3)$ as an exact polynomial identity in $(1/\omega_1,1/\omega_1')$. The "4" is the jet normalisation $M_{\rm vac}=2h^2P^3p_{02}$ per site, and $c$ arises from the frame tie (\ref{eq:kappaG}) exactly.

## General $\Lambda$: $[3,1,0]$ and $[3,2,0]$ {#sec:jetgen}

The same fit pipeline, now with the sparse hypothesis tested first, gave the generalisation. For $[3,2,0]$ (dim 15, 225 states) with $c=\prod_\omega(\zeta_2-\omega)(\zeta_3-\omega)^3(\zeta_1-\zeta_2)^4$ and $M=P^3p_{03}$, the target is exactly (residual $0.0$ at 80 digits) a bilinear form in $P^3$ times the seven non-forced coordinates $\{p_{03},p_{04},p_{13},p_{14},p_{23},p_{24},p_{34}\}$ per site; the kernel is unique (49 unknowns, rank 49 on 1125 rows), rational, and equal for every $\zeta$ point to $\sim10^{-72}$. Dropping any one of the seven leaves a residual ($0.41$ without $p_{03}$ or $p_{04}$, $0.16,0.25,0.078,0.14,0.061$ for $p_{13},p_{14},p_{23},p_{24},p_{34}$). For $[3,1,0]$ ($c=(\zeta_2-\omega)^2(\zeta_3-\omega)^3(\zeta_1-\zeta_2)^2$ per vacuum, $M=P^3p_{02}$), greedy backward elimination from 18 features ends with the pure Plücker basis of the nine non-forced pairs, 81 unknowns, rank 81, residual $0.0$, unique rational kernel, $K_{99}=1/9$; the adjoint-like five-element basis fails ($0.316$). The pattern is the count
$$
\#\text{monomials}=\binom{\lambda_1+2}2-\binom{\lambda_2+1}2=6-1,\ 10-1,\ 10-3=5,\ 9,\ 7.\label{eq:count}
$$
In the $\nu$-variables of $[3,2,0]$ the seven monomials are $(1,\kappa,\kappa_2)\times(1,\pi_4)$ and $\pi_{34}$ with $\pi_4=p_{04}/p_{03}$, $\pi_{34}=p_{34}/p_{03}$; monomials of $\nu$-weight $\le3$ (13 of them) fail ($0.0046$), weight $\le4$ fit.^[Agent P4, `RESULTS-Qside-320.md` section J (hypothesis ladder table, $[3,1,0]$ comparison T7), points $P,P',X_1,X_2,X_3$ built at 80 digits; the wrong exponents of $c$ ($(1,3,2)$ for $[3,1,0]$) give $0.32$.] The kernel is neither symmetric at fixed $\theta_{12}$ nor does $K+K^T$ express site exchange; the exchange symmetry is $K_{ij}(\omega,\omega,1/\theta_{12})=K_{ji}(\omega,\omega,-1/\theta_{12})$ (deviation $5.8\cdot10^{-63}$).

## Kernel laws {#sec:laws}

Table~\ref{tab:laws} collects the laws that each kernel obeys. They were established on grids of $(\omega_1,\omega_1')$ (9 values, 72 ordered pairs, 5 twist points each) and $\theta_{12}$ (12 distinct values) with exact rational polynomial reconstruction, and the structure was verified at held-out points; Appendix~\ref{app:K} gives the data. The two sites exchange under $\theta_{12}\to-\theta_{12}$, and the first non-forced coordinate carries weight $0$, with the monomial weight $e_{kl}=k+l-\lambda_2-1$.

